# Chapter: Compose - drive the lint dispatcher from lmscript
# Shows: system argv, exit-code asserts, counting findings in stdout
# Run: lmscript examples/lint-repo.lms      (needs lmok on PATH, e.g. PATH=build:$PATH)
# Needs: README setup; repo root, build/ present, lmok on PATH; offline after setup.
# exit: 0
# expect:
#|repo lint: c-security 1 findings, json-config 2 findings

# The lint dispatcher is a plain CLI operation; its stdout is ordinary data.
r1 = system(["lmok", "lint", "examples/rules/c-security.json", "examples/data/sample.c"]);
assert(r1.code == 0);
r2 = system(["lmok", "lint", "examples/rules/json-config.json", "examples/data/bad-config.json"]);
assert(r2.code == 0);

println("repo lint: c-security " + str(count_matches(r1.stdout, "\"rule\":")) + " findings, json-config " + str(count_matches(r2.stdout, "\"rule\":")) + " findings");
